 r←GetReadmeUrls(projectUrl version);ver;group;repo;path;tag;filename;filenames;branchRef
⍝ Returns a three-column matrix with the URLs a package's README might be fetched from:
⍝ [;1] the "raw.githubusercontent.com" URL to fetch it from
⍝ [;2] the matching "github.com/.../blob/..." URL, recorded for attributing the source
⍝ [;3] 'tag' or 'branch': which of the two the row is keyed on, carried through so that the
⍝      package page can say where the text actually came from
⍝ Rows come in the order they are worth trying, and every tag row comes before every branch
⍝ row: a README fetched from the tag documents this very release, while one fetched from
⍝ the default branch documents whatever the project looks like today. The branch rows are
⍝ there for the repositories that carry no tag for the version - without them those
⍝ packages could never show a README at all - and `GetReadmeSection` says which of the two
⍝ a package ended up with, so nobody is told that today's text describes this release.
⍝ Tatin release tags read "v1.2.3", but tags older than that convention read "1.2.3", and
⍝ GitHub serves raw files case sensitively, so each ref is tried with every spelling of the
⍝ filename that occurs in the wild. "README.md" is tried against both tags before any other
⍝ spelling is tried at all: it is what almost every repository uses, and that keeps the
⍝ first request unchanged for the packages this already works for.
⍝ "HEAD" stands for the repository's default branch whatever it happens to be called, and
⍝ raw.githubusercontent.com and github.com both accept it, so the name need not be looked
⍝ up - which would take an API call, and the GitHub API allows only 60 an hour without a
⍝ token.
⍝ The result is empty when `projectUrl` does not point at a GitHub repository: nothing else
⍝ is supported, and guessing would attach a stranger's README to a package.
 r←0 3⍴''
 filenames←'README.md' 'README.MD' 'ReadMe.md' 'readme.md'
 branchRef←'HEAD'
 ver←version
 ver←(¯1+ver⍳'+')↑ver                               ⍝ Build metadata is no part of a tag
 path←projectUrl
 :If 0=≢ver
 :OrIf 0=≢path
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :If '/'=¯1↑path                                    ⍝ A trailing slash is common and harmless
     path←¯1↓path
 :EndIf
 :If '.git'≡⎕C ¯4↑path
     path←¯4↓path
 :EndIf
 :If 0=≢path←GetGitHubPath path
     :Return
 :EndIf
 (group repo)←path
 :For filename :In filenames
     :For tag :In ('v',ver)ver
         r⍪←(GetRawGitHubUrl group repo tag filename)(GetBlobGitHubUrl group repo tag filename)'tag'
     :EndFor
 :EndFor
 :For filename :In filenames
     r⍪←(GetRawGitHubUrl group repo branchRef filename)(GetBlobGitHubUrl group repo branchRef filename)'branch'
 :EndFor
⍝Done
